<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<exercise xml:id="problem-closed-sets-in-subspaces" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    Closed sets in subspaces
  </title>
  
  <statement>
    <p>
      Let <m> U \subseteq X </m> be a subset of a topological space <m> \of{ X , \tau } </m>. Prove that a subset <m> W \subseteq U </m> is closed in <m> U </m> if and only if <m> W = U \cap V </m> for some closed set <m> V \subseteq X </m> in <m> X </m>.
    </p>
  </statement>
  
  <!-- <solution>
    <p>
      Fix a subset <m> W \subseteq U </m> of <m> U </m>, and suppose first that <m> W </m> is closed in <m> U </m>. Then <m> U \setminus W \in \rest{ \tau }_{ U } </m> is open in <m> U </m>, and so <m> U \setminus W = U \cap Y </m> for some open set <m> Y \in \tau </m> in <m> X </m>. Let <m> V = X \setminus Y </m>, and note that <m> V </m> is closed in <m> X </m>. Moreover,
      
      <md>
        <mrow>
          W \amp = U \setminus \of{ U \setminus W } = U \setminus \of{ U \cap Y }
        </mrow>
        
        <mrow>
          \amp = \of{ U \setminus U } \cup \of{ U \setminus Y } = \emptyset \cup \setmid{ u \in U }{ u \notin Y }
        </mrow>
        
        <mrow>
          \amp = \setmid{ x \in X }{ x \in U \textrm{ and } x \notin Y } = U \cap \setmid{ x \in X }{ x \notin Y }
        </mrow>
        
        <mrow>
          \amp = U \cap \of{ X \setminus Y } = U \cap V
        </mrow>
      </md>.
    </p>
    
    <p>
      Conversely, now suppose that <m> W = U \cap V </m> for some closed set <m> V \subseteq X </m> in <m> X </m>. Then <m> X \setminus V \in \tau </m> is open in <m> X </m>, and so
      
      <md>
        <mrow>
          U \setminus W = U \setminus \of{ U \cap V } = \of{ U \setminus U } \cup \of{ U \setminus V }
        </mrow>
        
        <mrow>
          \amp = \emptyset \cup \of{ U \cap \of{ X \setminus V } } = U \cap \of{ X \setminus V } \in \rest{ \tau }_{ U }
        </mrow>
      </md>
      
      is open in <m> U </m>. We conclude that <m> W </m> is closed in <m> U </m>.
    </p>
  </solution> -->
</exercise>
